{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nAt `72e58f613ab52a393c35b3225a51490b72364c62`, the 18 Python modules below contain 29 confirmed editable prose blocks (22 true leading docstrings, 7 maximal full-line comment regions; 3,265 before-words). The current-parent inventory remaps the env-helper comment to its `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_STEAL` assertion and includes the stale-count docstring in the CLI-reference mutation-verb test. The base SHA and stable IDs are immutable before-citations; line numbers are not scope.\n\n## Editing boundary\nEdit only the path-qualified stable IDs below plus adjacent blank-line normalization. `D:<owner>` means the leading `Expr(Constant(str))` of that exact module/class/function owner. `C:<scope>:before:<anchor>` means one maximal full-line comment region in the innermost AST scope, anchored to the next unchanged code prefix. The full ID is `<path>#<D-or-C-ID>`.\n\nFor every owned path, retain immutable-before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. Remove only allowlisted leading docstrings on comparison copies, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require the remaining ASTs equal. Tokenization must reject changed inline or non-allowlisted comments. Directive text and attachment are separately exact.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference_mutation_verbs.py` — `D:<module>`, `D:test_a_rewritten_sentence_fails_loudly_rather_than_silently`\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` — `D:test_every_known_env_helper_row_has_a_live_definition`, `D:test_stale_known_env_helper_r